WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.666
The face that changed: this is an original educational illustration, not a participant test.

00:00:06.666 --> 00:00:13.333
In 1980, Peter Thompson described a strange effect: an altered face looked less unusual upside down.

00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:20.000
The eyes and mouth are locally reversed inside an otherwise upright face.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:26.666
When the whole portrait is inverted, judging those differences can become harder.

00:00:26.666 --> 00:00:33.333
This concerns the orientation and relationships of facial features, not a magical power.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:40.000
What did your first glance fail to compare? Follow the evidence at Final Vestige.
